GUEST ARTICLE POINTS (each may help open the post, or appear once later as a short example):
- P1: Collecting information from websites by automated means has become a routine business activity rather than an occasional one-off task.
- P2: Companies gather public web pages to study competitors, track prices, follow customer reviews and understand what shoppers want.
- P3: The information gathered is only useful once it is cleaned up and put into a form that software can read and search.
- P4: Websites that build their pages on the fly are harder to read automatically, so organisations often need more than one method of collection.
- P5: Much of this work is now run through rented online services, so companies do not have to own and maintain the equipment themselves.
- P6: Automated collection is increasingly tied to artificial intelligence, which needs large amounts of clean, well-organised text to work well.

