      "Software can now pull readable text off websites and hand it to artificial intelligence systems, which use that text to learn and answer questions. Anyone weighing that task soon runs into a bigger question: where the text comes from, and who collects it. Automated collection of public web pages has become routine business work rather than an occasional chore. Companies gather pages to study competitors, track prices, follow customer reviews and learn what shoppers want. Much of the work now runs through rented online services, so a company does not have to own and maintain the equipment itself. That wider business of collecting web data is what the [[CMI_LINK:Web Scraping Services Market]] covers.",
      "[[SPONSOR_PARAGRAPH]]"
