          "paragraph": "Hybrid advisory pairs automated investing with a human advisor, and it is where much of the new competition sits. Edward Jones launched its Digital Managed Solutions robo advisor in August 2026 to reach young earners and savers who are just starting to invest, according to Financial Planning. The service asks for only $5,000 to begin, against minimums of $25,000 at Fidelity and $50,000 at Vanguard for their hybrid services. Edward Jones also said it would roll out a hybrid digital advice offering to make its wealth management platform more appealing to younger investors, as MSN reported in August 2026. A lower entry point widens the pool of clients a firm can serve, and it gives the wealth management platform market opportunities to sell into firms that want both automation and human backup."
