- Build the opening as: a lead-in paragraph that sets the scene with the subject and names the market through the report link, inside its first 100 words; then a second paragraph of your own in which the placeholder sits INSIDE one of your sentences, with your own words before and after it (the retained text is a short linked phrase, not a paragraph, so it never stands alone on a line). Nothing else is needed. The link is written exactly once, as [[CMI_LINK:Digital Marketing Software Market]], and it is the first time the market's name appears.
- The opening states no market fact (no size, growth, share, segment or vendor).

THE TRANSITION (about 101 words, one or two short paragraphs, no heading; never fewer than 75 words — a shorter transition vanishes between the opening and the sections and falls below the share the plan gives this block)
