QUESTION 1 (Q2): How fast is the digital marketing software market growing?
Facts this answer may use:
- Market forecast: USD 37.94 billion (2033)
- Growth rate (CAGR): 11.2% (2026 to 2033)

QUESTION 2 (Q3): What are the latest trends in digital marketing software?
Facts this answer may use:
- The integration of AI and machine learning in marketing solutions enhances personalization and campaign effectiveness, with AI users achieving up to 30% higher conversion rates in 2026.
- Rising global digital advertising expenditure fuels adoption, with Asia Pacific digital ad spends growing 19% annually between 2024 and 2026.
- The shift to omnichannel marketing requires sophisticated tools to unify cross-channel data, evidenced by a 25% increase in ROI among early adopters.
- Real-time analytics adoption reduces customer churn by 20%, boosting market growth.
- The average enterprise now runs over 90 marketing technology tools simultaneously, yet most CMOs admit they cannot clearly measure the ROI of more than half their stack. (source: mba-training.com, 2026-06)
- The marketing technology landscape has grown from 150 solutions in 2011 to 15,384 solutions, a 9% increase from 14,106, with 2,489 new tools qualifying in 2025 out of 11,133 candidates evaluated. (source: gtm8020.com, 2026-01)
    detail: The same compilation reports marketing budgets dropped to 7.7% of company revenue in 2024, down from 9.1% in 2023.
- A Gartner survey found that 78% of CMOs report feeling unprepared for the future of marketing technology. (source: cmonewsdesk.com, 2026-07)
    detail: The figure comes from Gartner's 2025-2026 CMO Spend and Strategy Survey, which the article says shows a disconnect between perceived need and actual investment, with most marketing budgets still heavi
- Interviews with 15 global CMOs surfaced five priorities reshaping marketing leadership in an AI-driven world, including transforming with and for AI and developing new metrics for zero-click AI platforms. (source: MIT Sloan Mgmt Review, 2026-09)
    detail: The MIT Sloan Management Review piece lists the other priorities as repositioning marketing within the enterprise, hiring amid disruption, and navigating an evolving media landscape.
- Stakewise, a New Zealand-based investment platform, saw ChatGPT generate roughly 700 referral sessions to its site each month by mid-2025, up from only a handful a year earlier. (source: MIT Sloan Mgmt Review, 2026-10)
    detail: Visitors arriving through ChatGPT had lower bounce rates and viewed more pages per visit than those from other referral sources, even though the site performed strongly on conventional SEO measures.
- Salesforce agreed to acquire marketing technology platform Braze for $47.50 a share in cash, valuing Braze at $5.66 billion including debt. (source: CNBC, 2026-10)
    detail: CNBC reports Salesforce is buying Braze to strengthen its marketing business, one of its weaker application verticals in recent quarters. Braze's real-time personalization capabilities, especially on 
- Salesforce made AI agents touchpoints in the customer journey as part of its Agentforce launch, tying them into its revenue engine and attribution models. (source: Forrester Blogs, 2026-10)
    detail: Forrester notes Salesforce's website produces 200 signals that feed attribution models and determine the next best experience for a visitor, and that the company aligned incentives so there was no pat

